```apex
/**
 * TDTM trigger handler that creates a follow-up task for major gifts.
 *
 * Register in NPSP Trigger Configuration:
 *   Class: OPP_MajorGiftFollowUp_TDTM
 *   Object: Opportunity
 *   Trigger Action: AfterInsert;AfterUpdate
 *   Load Order: 5
 *   Asynchronous: unchecked
 *
 * When an Opportunity becomes Closed Won with Amount >= 5000 (and was not
 * already both of those before the update), the handler hands a single
 * Task to the TDTM dispatcher via the returned DmlWrapper, so the insert
 * is executed by NPSP's framework as one bulkified DML statement.
 */
public class OPP_MajorGiftFollowUp_TDTM extends npsp.TDTM_Runnable {

    private static final String TASK_SUBJECT  = 'Major gift thank-you call';
    private static final String TASK_PRIORITY = 'High';
    private static final String TASK_STATUS   = 'Not Started';
    private static final Decimal MIN_AMOUNT   = 5000;
    private static final String STAGE_CLOSED_WON = 'Closed Won';

    public override npsp.TDTM_Runnable.DmlWrapper run(
        List<SObject> newlist,
        List<SObject> oldlist,
        npsp.TDTM_Runnable.Action triggerAction,
        Schema.DescribeSObjectResult objResult
    ) {
        npsp.TDTM_Runnable.DmlWrapper dmlWrapper = new npsp.TDTM_Runnable.DmlWrapper();

        if (newlist == null || newlist.isEmpty()) {
            return dmlWrapper;
        }

        if (triggerAction != npsp.TDTM_Runnable.Action.AfterInsert
                && triggerAction != npsp.TDTM_Runnable.Action.AfterUpdate) {
            return dmlWrapper;
        }

        Map<Id, Opportunity> oldOpps = new Map<Id, Opportunity>();
        if (oldlist != null) {
            for (SObject so : oldlist) {
                Opportunity o = (Opportunity) so;
                oldOpps.put(o.Id, o);
            }
        }

        List<Task> tasksToInsert = new List<Task>();

        for (SObject so : newlist) {
            Opportunity newOpp = (Opportunity) so;
            Opportunity oldOpp = oldOpps.get(newOpp.Id);

            // If the gift already qualified before this change, do not
            // create another task.
            if (oldOpp != null && qualifies(oldOpp)) {
                continue;
            }

            if (qualifies(newOpp)) {
                tasksToInsert.add(buildTask(newOpp));
            }
        }

        if (!tasksToInsert.isEmpty()) {
            dmlWrapper.recordsToInsert = tasksToInsert;
        }

        return dmlWrapper;
    }

    private static Task buildTask(Opportunity opp) {
        return new Task(
            Subject      = TASK_SUBJECT,
            Priority     = TASK_PRIORITY,
            Status       = TASK_STATUS,
            WhatId       = opp.Id,
            WhoId        = opp.npsp__Primary_Contact__c,
            OwnerId      = opp.OwnerId,
            ActivityDate = opp.CloseDate != null
                               ? opp.CloseDate.addDays(3)
                               : null
        );
    }

    /**
     * A gift qualifies when it is Closed Won with Amount >= 5000.
     * StageName is checked in addition to IsWon because the derived
     * IsWon flag may not be populated on in-memory SObject instances.
     */
    private static Boolean qualifies(Opportunity o) {
        if (o == null) {
            return false;
        }
        Boolean isWon = (o.IsWon == true) || STAGE_CLOSED_WON.equals(o.StageName);
        return isWon
            && o.Amount != null
            && o.Amount >= MIN_AMOUNT;
    }
}
```

**Root cause of the failures:** the tests (and NPSP's TDTM dispatcher) expect the handler to *return* its DML work in a `DmlWrapper` rather than executing `insert` itself. Because the previous version inserted internally and returned `null`, the dispatcher/caller never received the records — and the caller that executes `dmlWrapper.recordsToInsert` performed an empty insert, hence 0 tasks and the "List has no rows" query exception. The corrected version populates `dmlWrapper.recordsToInsert` with the (single, bulkified) task list, so the dispatcher performs exactly one DML statement per transaction, still uses no SOQL, never duplicates on already-qualified gifts, and respects the field mapping (Subject, Priority, Status, WhatId, WhoId from `npsp__Primary_Contact__c`, OwnerId, CloseDate + 3 days).

